## Reusable support snippet =E2=80=94 Exit Load on Mutual Fund Redemption

- Exit load is a fee some mutual fund schemes charge when you redeem units be=
fore a defined holding period.
- It is charged by the fund scheme, not by Groww, and is deducted from your r=
edemption proceeds.
- It is calculated as a percentage of the redeemed value, so the credited amo=
unt can be lower than the value shown.
- Each scheme sets its own exit load and holding period; check the scheme's S=
cheme Information Document.
- For most equity schemes the holding period is 1 year, but this varies by sc=
heme.
- There is no exit load after the holding period defined by the scheme.

